WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.120
- [Instructor] So I have a
rectangle drawn right over here.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.660
And my goal is to split this rectangle up

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.970
into smaller, equal squares.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:11.920
And the way that I'm going to do that

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.920
is by first dividing this
rectangle into two rows,

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.630
and I should say two equal rows.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.500
And then I'm going to
divide this rectangle

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.030
into five equal columns.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.237
Now, I know some of you are saying,

00:00:28.237 --> 00:00:30.890
"What is a row and what is a column?"

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.440
So a row, at least my
brain thinks about it

00:00:34.308 --> 00:00:39.308
as a part of the rectangle that
is going from left to right.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:40.976
One way to think about it,

00:00:40.976 --> 00:00:43.876
if I had a bunch of, let's say
that these are apples here.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.160
And if I wanted to think about dividing

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.010
these apples into rows,

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.000
I would say that this is the first row.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.860
This is a second row.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.280
And that this is a third row.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.220
If I were to think in terms of columns,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.610
I tend to think of
columns as going up down.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.310
And so the columns, this
would be one column.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.220
This would be another column.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.840
This would be a third column,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.230
and this would be a fourth column.

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:15.070
So now that we understand
what rows and columns are,

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.330
let's first think about,

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.810
maybe pause this video and
think about how would you divide

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.713
this rectangle into two rows.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.780
Well, the way that I would tackle it is,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.010
I would draw a line that
goes from left to right,

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.260
and there you have it.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.260
I now have the rectangle
split into one row

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.360
and now a second row.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.210
Now pause the video
and you could draw this

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.790
if you have a pencil and paper with you,

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.080
or you could just think
about what I should do.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.433
How would I now divide this
rectangle into five columns?

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:50.767
Well, what I could do
is make a bunch of lines

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:53.000
that go from top to bottom.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.200
So that's one column there.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.043
This is a second column.

00:01:59.748 --> 00:02:01.840
This is a third column.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:06.840
This is a fourth column
and a fifth column.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.253
So there you have it.

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:11.100
I have two rows, one row, two rows,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.260
and I have five columns.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:16.000
One, two, three, four, five.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.210
Now what's interesting is
when I split the rectangle

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.930
in this way into two
rows and five columns,

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.873
how many equal size squares did I create?

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.140
Well, I've created one,
two, three, four, five,

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.300
six, seven, eight, nine, 10 equal squares.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:38.060
And that makes sense
because each row has five.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.550
I have one, two, three, four, five.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.800
One, two, three, four, five.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.230
And five plus five is equal to 10.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.350
Another way to think about
it is each column has two,

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:57.350
one, two, one, two, one,
two, one two, one, two.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.100
And two plus two is four,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:05.100
plus two is six, plus two
is eight, plus two is 10.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.200
So that's what splitting
the rectangle into two rows

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.760
and five columns gets me,

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.263
it splits it into 10 sections.

